caramos-app-center (0.2.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * An app installs while another package is broken (ticket H-1094). When
    dpkg could not finish a package, an NVIDIA 470 driver whose module does
    not build on Linux 6.14 for instance, apt-get configured it again on
    every install and failed, so every app failed too. An app that got
    installed now counts as installed, with the broken packages in its log;
    when it did not get installed, the page names the packages dpkg could
    not finish and, for an NVIDIA driver, points to Driver Check.
  * Installing on the live USB while the CaramOS installer runs (ticket
    H-1091). The installer keeps debconf locked, so packages that ask a
    debconf question (Microsoft fonts) failed with "config.dat is locked":
    such an install now waits for the lock, up to 15 minutes, and tries
    once more, or says another program is installing software; other apps
    install meanwhile without waiting. A failed apt-get update (the CD-ROM
    source the installer adds, another program's repository) no longer
    stops an install: apt installs from the lists it has.
  * Downloads that the server cuts off go on (tickets H-1091 and H-1096).
    curl --retry does not repeat "Connection reset by peer" (curl exit 56),
    which the WPS Office server often sends: a recipe download now tries
    up to five times and continues from the bytes it already has.

 -- Vietnam Linux Family <developer@vietnamlinuxfamily.net>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 11:09:13 +0700

caramos-app-center (0.2.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Zalo installs again (tickets H-1039 and H-1060). Zalo for Linux 26.10.11
    makes voice and video calls with its own Linux engine and no longer
    publishes the Wine-based "Full" build the recipe looked for, so every
    Zalo install failed. The recipe now installs the newest ZaDark x86_64
    build, falling back to an older release when the newest one lacks it,
    and installs python3, libopus0 and pulseaudio-utils for calls when
    they are missing. The card says about 170 MB and calls without Wine.
  * A failed install says why. The helper reports the last line a recipe
    printed (its own message, curl or apt-get) instead of "exited with 1",
    and the page after a failed install shows that reason instead of always
    blaming the network connection.
  * "Ask for help" ("Nhờ giúp đỡ") after a failed install or removal opens
    Feedback & Help (caramos-help, from caramos-ota) with a bug report
    started and the failed apps' installer output attached, for the VNLF
    team only; Feedback & Help takes personal data out of it first.

 -- Vietnam Linux Family <developer@vietnamlinuxfamily.net>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:45:00 +0700

